{"response":"Based on the current offers I found, the strongest personal-card sign-up bonus is the EcoCard: earn 2,000 sustainability points—worth $20 when redeemed as a statement or checking-account credit—after spending $5,000 in eligible purchases during your first month. The offer runs through December 15, 2025. It has no stated credit-score requirement, but it carries a $50 annual fee and a 19.99% purchase APR, so it’s most attractive if you can meet the spending requirement and pay the balance in full.

If you’re applying for a business card, the Business Silver Rewards Card has a potentially larger ongoing promotional benefit: 2× cash back for the first six months, including 20% on travel and software purchases that normally earn 10%, and 2% on other purchases that normally earn 1%. The promotional window ends today, November 14, 2025, and the offer requires opening the account during that window.

For a straightforward personal sign-up bonus, I’d start with the EcoCard. For a business with substantial travel or software spending, the Business Silver offer could be more valuable. I can narrow this down further if you tell me whether you want a personal or business card and roughly how much you expect to spend in the first month."}
